Writing a `package.json` with `type: "module"` inside `.git/hooks` is risky because `.git/hooks` is a shared directory. If a developer has other custom or third-party Node.js hooks (e.g., Husky) written in CommonJS, they will break.

We can avoid this entirely by writing the generated wrapper as a CommonJS script (using `require` and wrapping the dynamic `import()` in an IIFE), which eliminates the need to write `package.json` in `.git/hooks`.

